    "_was": "\\bcurl\\s+.*\\|\\s*(?:bash|sh|zsh)\\b",
    "_why_changed": "Unbounded .* before the pipe: on 'curl ' repeated through a 100k input the engine ran .* to end-of-text and backtracked, at every start \u2014 2.8s for one rule. The negated class excludes '|' itself, so the greedy run stops exactly at the pipe and there is no split to retry. Same idiom LLM08_pipe_exec already uses.",
    "_bounds_tightened": "Cost of this shape is (start positions x wildcard bound); with the leading verb repeated through a 100k input the bound is the only lever. Tightened to keep one rule's worst case in the low hundreds of ms; still spans any real single-command invocation."
